# {{ itsm_kb_vm_provisioning_title }}

## New stack deploy — launch workflow directly

When the user asks to deploy a new Generic Application stack, collect stack parameters and launch **{{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_workflow }}** (org **{{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_organization }}**). **Do not ask** for `itsm_change_ref` or `itsm_service_request_ref` — the workflow creates and submits the ITSM service request and standard change automatically on the first step.

| Extra var | Req | Source |
|-----------|-----|--------|
| `vm_name` | yes | User |
| `cpus` | yes | User |
| `mem` | yes | User |
| `app_repo` | yes | User (full Gitea repo URL, e.g. `{{ itsm_kb_vm_provisioning_example_app_repo }}`) |
| `app_branch` | no | User, optional |
| `app_packages` | yes | User (comma-separated RPMs, e.g. `httpd,git`) |
| `app_clone_path` | yes | User (e.g. `/var/www/html`) |
| `app_service` | yes | User (systemd unit, e.g. `httpd`) |

Example (no REQ/CHG — workflow opens ITSM objects):

```
vm_name: server01
cpus: 2
mem: 4
app_repo: {{ itsm_kb_vm_provisioning_example_app_repo }}
app_branch: main
app_packages: httpd,git
app_clone_path: /var/www/html
app_service: httpd
```

Job template "{{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_workflow }}"

## Optional — manual ITSM catalog submit first

Operators may still open catalog **{{ itsm_generic_app_stack_request_template_name }}** in itsm-app and submit before launching the workflow. If `itsm_change_ref` and `itsm_service_request_ref` are already known, pass them in the workflow survey; the auto-submit step is skipped.

For **incident remediation** (`[incident.created]`, Generic application down, `INC-*`): **do not use this article or workflow {{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_workflow }}**. Follow **{{ itsm_kb_generic_app_incident_remediation_title }}** and launch job template **{{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_jt_remediate_incident }}** with `vm_name` and `itsm_incident_ref` only.

For **stack deletion**: follow **{{ itsm_kb_generic_app_deletion_title }}** and launch workflow **{{ aap_generic_app_delete_pipeline_workflow }}** (never **{{ aap_generic_app_stack_pipeline_workflow }}**).

